#: data/io.github.cheviiot.alcove.metainfo.xml.in:28
msgid ""
"Alcove is a GNOME-native manager for isolated web applications. WebKitGTK is "
"the default engine, and Chromium is available as a Flatpak add-on for "
"explicitly selected sites. Each website gets separate local data, cookies, "
"cache, settings, and its own desktop launcher."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.alcove.metainfo.xml.in:34
msgid ""
"Alcove is an independent successor to Spider. The original work by Zaedus, "
"Cameron Radmore's contribution, and their Git history remain credited. "
"Alcove is developed independently and does not claim their endorsement or "
"participation."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.alcove.metainfo.xml.in:41
msgid "Create, edit, repair, and remove portal-installed launchers"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.alcove.metainfo.xml.in:42
msgid ""
"Fetch and safely normalize website icons, with a working fallback when the "
"site offers none"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.alcove.metainfo.xml.in:43
msgid ""
"Keep each application's configuration, policy, profile, and cache separate"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.alcove.metainfo.xml.in:58
msgid "Turn any valid HTTP(S) address into an isolated desktop application"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.alcove.metainfo.xml.in:59
msgid "Keep each site's profile, cookies, cache and storage separate"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.alcove.metainfo.xml.in:60
msgid "Use WebKitGTK by default and offer Chromium as an optional add-on"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.cheviiot.alcove.metainfo.xml.in:61
msgid "Integrate with GNOME through desktop portals and encrypted backups"
